<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shunzhi Emperor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shunzhi Emperor was the first emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Dynasty</a> to rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, enthroned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> in 1644 while still a child. During his reign, regents and generals continued campaigns against Ming loyalists in the south. The Qing Empire profile places his reign at the start of Qing rule in China.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shunzhi-emperor.jpg" alt="Shunzhi Emperor" width="256" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B8%85%E4%B8%96%E7%A5%96%E9%A1%BA%E6%B2%BB%E7%9A%87%E5%B8%9D%E6%9C%9D%E6%9C%8D%E5%83%8F.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
